OL,3,GNEWSAPet loss stigma 'makes owners
OL,4,Adownplay their grief'
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe vast majority of owners say stigma
OL,7,Faround pet loss makes them downplay
OL,8,Ftheir grief to family and friends, a
OL,9,Fnew survey reveals.
OL,11,FMore than 70% of the 4,000 people who
OL,12,Ftook part in the RSPCA's research
OL,13,Fbelieve pet grief is not taken
OL,14,Fseriously, which is why the animal
OL,15,Fcharity has launched a "Not Just a Pet"
OL,16,Fcampaign.
OL,18,FSuzanne Norbury from Bristol said after
OL,19,Fher "cherished" rescue cat Penny died
OL,20,Fin 2025, the emptiness was
OL,21,F"overwhelming".
OL,23,APub: 09-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBW-SW Eng NewsC Reg TVFWeather
